&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re standing up a new function at Alloy: Forward Deployed Engineering. Our largest enterprise customers need a trusted technical partner with a strong point of view on how Alloy fits into their tech stack and fraud strategy. As a Forward Deployed Engineer, you&#39;ll be that partner - embedded with our most strategic accounts and owning the technical outcome end-to-end, with each deployment becoming the foundation for the next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be one of the first two engineers on this founding team. This is a software engineering role through and through - based within our Engineering org, with a scope that spans software, product, and solutions engineering. You won&#39;t just join this function - you&#39;ll define how it works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alloy operates in a hybrid-work environment. We look to foster collaboration and community by having our local employees onsite three days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and tune customer and channel-partner deployments end-to-end — API integrations, third-party data integrations, SDKs, and latency constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write production code across our stack: TypeScript, JavaScript (ES6/React), Python (Django), Node.js, PostgreSQL, OpenSearch, and AWS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as Alloy&#39;s credible technical voice with customer engineering leadership, making architectural calls in real time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the engineering track of QBRs for your accounts and serve in their on-call escalation path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn your work into reusable platform primitives and docs, so each deployment makes the next one faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of hands-on experience developing production-ready software, with a proven track record of delivering robust, scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a customer-facing technical role, Forward Deployed Engineering, solutions engineering with deep technical ownership, or similar - where you were accountable to an external stakeholder, not just an internal roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong backend and API fluency, with the ability to read and write production code across services you don&#39;t own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound architectural judgment under ambiguity: you can make and defend technical decisions in the room, with a customer watching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine pull toward customer-facing work - you find energy in solving a real customer&#39;s real problem, alongside their engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear technical communicator who can explain a complex integration tradeoff to a bank&#39;s VP of Engineering and to an Alloy PM in the same afternoon.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel on occasion to our NYC office, as well as client offices in the US.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a company with a strong Forward Deployed Engineering culture (Palantir, Scale AI, Ramp, Plaid, Stripe, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with identity, fraud, KYC/KYB, or financial services infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SDK development or embedded front-end integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a lean team, so your impact will be felt immediately, and opportunities will grow as the company scales up. If this all sounds like a good fit for you, why not join us?&lt;/p&gt;
