&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Revenue Operations runs the systems and data that Sales, Marketing, and Customer Success depend on to find, win, and keep customers. GTM Systems is the technical core of that team. Every quote, every routing rule, and every pipeline number traces back to architecture this function builds. The stack is growing alongside the business, and the person who owns it decides what it becomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alloy operates in a hybrid-work environment. We look to foster collaboration and community by having our local employees onsite three days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own the architecture, build, and administration of Alloy&#39;s revenue tech stack. This role is built for someone who stays technical: you set the direction for GTM systems and you write the automations and architect the integrations yourself. You&#39;ll report to the VP of Revenue Operations and partner closely with Sales, Marketing, Customer Success, Product, and Finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the architecture, roadmap, and day to day administration of Alloy&#39;s core GTM systems, including Salesforce, Gong, &lt;a href=&quot;http://Apollo.io&quot;&gt;Apollo.io&lt;/a&gt;, and adjacent tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain integrations and automations across the GTM stack using APIs and iPaaS platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the data model and integration architecture connecting GTM systems to downstream tooling such as Netsuite and Snowflake.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own system reliability and data integrity across the stack. Troubleshoot issues directly and drive them to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently drive automation that improves GTM team productivity and data hygiene, from identifying the opportunity through to shipping it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales Ops and Deal Desk on quote to cash, approvals, and territory and quota automation so the stack scales with headcount growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, select, and manage GTM tooling vendors, including renewals and platform consolidation decisions, alongside the VP of Revenue Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical standards for systems work and align with the GTM Engineer on architecture ownership so build effort is not duplicated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in systems administration, GTM engineering, revenue operations, or a similar technical role in SaaS, with deep hands-on Salesforce architecture and administration experience. Admin or Architect certification is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of personally designing and building integrations and automations rather than directing others to build them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with iPaaS platforms such as n8n, &lt;a href=&quot;http://Tray.io&quot;&gt;Tray.io&lt;/a&gt;, Workato, or Zapier, plus working knowledge of SQL and at least one scripting language (Python or JavaScript).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a GTM tech stack end to end at a scaling B2B SaaS company, including data warehousing concepts and BI tools such as Looker, Tableau, or dbt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The range to act as a strategic partner to RevOps leadership and as the engineer who ships the solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear cross-functional communication. You can turn a business requirement into systems logic and explain the tradeoffs back to the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, financial services, or another highly regulated industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity administering sales engagement tools, customer success platforms, and CPQ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring a systems analyst as a function has grown.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
