&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Talent Acquisition team shapes who Alloy becomes. We sit close to leadership, we treat sourcing as a craft, and we care about precision over volume. This is not a fill-the-req function: what we build here determines how Engineering, Product, and GTM get built. Alloy operates in a hybrid-work environment. We look to foster collaboration and community by having our local employees onsite three days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The best hires rarely come from a job post. They come from someone who found them first. You&#39;ll own outbound sourcing at Alloy, leading on Engineering searches while supporting Product and GTM, and you&#39;ll own how AI-powered sourcing gets done here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own sourcing strategy for Engineering roles and support Product and GTM searches, building talent maps of the strongest candidates in our key hiring areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write outreach that people with options actually answer: specific, credible, personalized, and worth their time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run parallel pipelines across competing roles, independently and in close partnership with TA partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source beyond LinkedIn: technical communities, open source contributions, research papers, referral networks, and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn market research into intelligence the team acts on, from competitive landscapes to emerging talent pools to what candidates are asking about.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track outreach conversion and pipeline metrics, report pipeline health clearly to recruiters and leadership, and iterate on what the data tells you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own our AI-augmented sourcing workflow, putting tools like &lt;a href=&quot;http://Noon.ai&quot;&gt;Noon.ai&lt;/a&gt; and Gem to work, using automation to extend your reach rather than replace your judgment, and codifying playbooks and talent maps the team adopts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of sourcing or research-focused recruiting experience, ideally at a high-growth tech company or fintech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record sourcing top talent (Data Science, Software Engineering, Security, Product, G&amp;amp;A, and GTM) with a strong emphasis on passive candidate engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real AI fluency: you&#39;ve put agentic sourcing tools to work in live searches, and you know where AI extends your reach and where your judgment wins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level command of LinkedIn Recruiter, including advanced Boolean, InMail strategy, and pipeline tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Gem and a clear understanding of how sourcing integrates with an ATS like Greenhouse or Ashby.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You track your numbers and iterate on them, and your outreach to technical audiences reads like it came from a person, not a sequence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running market research to inform sourcing strategy and talent mapping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience sourcing GTM roles (Sales, Marketing, Customer Success).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background building sourcing programs or channel strategies from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve configured agentic AI sourcing workflows that actually run, beyond off-the-shelf defaults.&lt;/li&gt;
